Your pets follow you more than the follow any one monster.
Move away from that watchman and chances are your pet
will lose interest in the attack without killing the watchman.
Note that on the way back up from mines end your pet may
be so powerful it can quickly kill regular watchmen and
survive doing so.

> Because they (the pets) thought they (the pets) could take them (the
> watchmen).

Pets don't take a monster's armor or weapons into account.

Often the watchmen and watch captain are the first well
armored and well weaponed monsters your pet encounters.
Thus the watch can survive combat with your pet longer than
other victims.  Your pets will retreat if they are hurt much and
monsters pursue you not your pet.  A monster using a good
weapon and cause damage so quickly your pet does not retreat
in time.  I lose plenty of pets in minetown because of this.

There are also certain monsters that hit very hard compared
to how easy they are to kill.  If your pet decides to attack
one it can end up quite random which dies first.  I recently
lost a pet to the first zrufty I encountered because of how hard
zrufties hit.

Above I suggested one way to reduce this risk.  Another
thing I do is try to herd the watch into rooms and lock the
doors as soon as I find a key.  That only lasts until digging
monsters let them out.



